s-incorrect-mac-says","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-25T19:44:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Chris Creighton out as coach at Eastern Michigan after 13 seasons","description":"Chris Creighton is out as head coach at Eastern Michigan after 13 seasons with the school.","published":"2026-11-25T19:05:05.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50595706/creighton-coach-eastern-michigan-13-seasons","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge denies SEC's request for TRO against LSU in Dec. 3 vote","description":"A federal judge denied the SEC's request for a temporary restraining order to keep LSU from interfering with a Dec. 3 vote of presidents and chancellors on whether to remove the school from the conference.","published":"2026-11-25T20:02:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50595702/judge-denies-sec-request-tro-lsu-dec-3-vote","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079698/ellis-robinson-iv","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellis_Robinson_IV"},"pick":{"pick":12,"round":1,"team":"LV","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Ellis Robinson IV","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellis_Robinson_IV","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-25T17:06:51Z","intro":"Ellis Robinson IV is an American college football cornerback for the Georgia Bulldogs of the Southeastern Conference (SEC). He was one of the top players in the 2024 class.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Robinson IV attended IMG Academy in Bradenton, Florida. As a sophomore attending Iona Prep, Robinson IV recorded 28 tackles and eight interceptions, before transferring to IMG Academy. Following his junior season, he was ranked as the number one collegiate prospect in the country by ESPN. A five-star recruit, Robinson IV committed to play college football at the University of Georgia over offers from Alabama, Colorado, LSU, and Miami."}]}}